StudySync is complete: an offline React + TypeScript (strict) + Vite app that turns subjects, exam dates, topics, availability and commitments into a deterministic study timetable. It uses an earliest-deadline-first scheduler with a documented priority heuristic, capacity-conflict reporting, regeneration with an added/moved/removed preview that keeps completed, locked and in-progress sessions, missed-session rescheduling (single and bulk) that keeps session identity, a dashboard, progress tracking, a versioned mock-test prompt builder (v1–final, observed results left empty), export/import with strict validation, schema migration and a recovery screen. After a clean `npm ci`, `npm run verify` passed on 2026-11-22: tsc 0 errors, eslint 0 warnings, Vitest 129/129 across 15 files (including fast-check invariants), vite build OK, and Playwright 29/29 (end-to-end flows, axe with no serious or critical violations, and no overflow from 360 to 1440 px). The production preview served the app, and `npm run package` produced studysync.zip.
